Built a stdlib-only `compress.py` that round-trips `corpus.txt` via `python3 compress.py corpus.txt out.bin` and `python3 compress.py --decompress out.bin restored.txt`. It tries zlib, bz2, and several lzma presets, stores a tiny header with the chosen method and original size, and verifies size on decompression. Manual check showed byte-identical restoration and compression to 20,793 bytes versus zlib default’s 35,399 bytes on the fixed corpus, i.e. about 93.38% reduction vs 88.73% baseline. Registered an assay for round-trip correctness plus percentage reduction, then tested multiple `compress.py` variants; none beat the incumbent, so the best version was kept.